# Android Fleet Inventory  (Phase 1 — host-side scheduled runner)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The human-editable source of truth for "what each device should be".
# Copy this file to  fleet/inventory.conf  and edit for your fleet.
# (inventory.conf is git-ignored so your real IPs stay out of the repo.)
#
# One device per line. Columns are whitespace-separated:
#
#   name       target             profile  app_set  debloat  degoogle  enabled  [mdns]
#
#   name      Friendly label used in logs/notifications.
#   target    host[:port] the runner reaches over wireless ADB. Port defaults
#             to 5555. Give the device a static IP / DHCP reservation.
#   profile   Device config profile applied every run (drift correction).
#             One of: profiles/<profile>.conf  (m11, m9, samsung, default, ...).
#   app_set   App set whose apps are installed/upgraded every run, or "none".
#             Prefer app-sets that use fdroid: sources — those auto-resolve the
#             latest version each run. (See docs/fleet-runner.md.)
#   debloat   Debloat tier re-applied every run (light|standard|aggressive) or
#             "none". Day-2 default is "none" — debloat is an onboarding step.
#   degoogle  1 to also remove Google apps during debloat, else 0. Ignored
#             when debloat=none.
#   enabled   1 to include this device in fleet runs, 0 to skip it.
#   mdns      OPTIONAL. The device's mDNS service name (from `adb mdns services`,
#             e.g. adb-XXXXXXXX-YYYYYY._adb-tls-connect._tcp). Used as a fallback
#             when the static target is unreachable (e.g. after a reboot changed
#             the Wireless-debugging port). Leave off if you don't use it.
#
# Blank lines and #-comments are ignored. Columns must not contain spaces.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# name        target              profile  app_set  debloat  degoogle  enabled
m11-wall      192.168.1.60:5555   m11      none     none     0         1
m9-wall       192.168.1.61:5555   m9       none     none     0         1

# Example with an app set that auto-updates (fdroid: sources) and mDNS fallback:
# office-tab   192.168.1.62:5555   default  minimal  none     0         1        adb-0A1B2C3D-4E5F6G._adb-tls-connect._tcp
